only the foreground color without pattern. Number in the interval [0,
1], or a vector of these.}

\item{edgeshape}{Determines which shape is used for edges between
`barpath` labels. One of \code{">"}, \code{"<"}, \code{"|"},
\code{"/"}, \code{"\\\\"}.}

\item{flip}{Determines if the positions obtained from solver are flipped
on each axis. Any combination of \code{"x"}, \code{"y"} joined with
\code{"+"}.}

\item{pad}{Sets the inner padding (in px). Number in the interval [0,
Inf].}
}
\value{
Each \code{go_*()} function returns a graph object of the same
  class as its name; \code{add_*()} functions return the modified figure.
}
\description{
Visualize hierarchal data from leaves (and/or outer branches) towards
root with rectangles. The icicle sectors are determined by the entries in
"labels" or "ids" and in "parents".
}
\details{
\code{go_icicle()} and the nested object constructors below create
validated graph objects (named lists). Every property is checked against
the plotly.js schema when an object is created or modified (see
\code{\link{plotly_obj-modify}()}). \code{add_icicle()} creates an object
and adds it to a figure.

Nested objects documented here:
\describe{
\item{\code{go_icicle_domain()}}{\code{icicle.domain}}
\item{\code{go_icicle_hoverlabel()}}{\code{icicle.hoverlabel}}
\item{\code{go_icicle_hoverlabel_font()}}{\code{icicle.hoverlabel.font}:
Sets the font used in hover labels.}
\item{\code{go_icicle_insidetextfont()}}{\code{icicle.insidetextfont}:
Sets the font used for `textinfo` lying inside the sector.}
\item{\code{go_icicle_leaf()}}{\code{icicle.leaf}}
\item{\code{go_icicle_legendgrouptitle()}}{\code{icicle.legendgrouptitle}}
\item{\code{go_icicle_legendgrouptitle_font()}}{\code{icicle.legendgrouptitle.font}:
Sets this legend group's title font.}
\item{\code{go_icicle_marker()}}{\code{icicle.marker}}
\item{\code{go_icicle_marker_colorbar()}}{\code{icicle.marker.colorbar}}
\item{\code{go_icicle_marker_colorbar_tickfont()}}{\code{icicle.marker.colorbar.tickfont}:
Sets the color bar's tick label font}
\item{\code{go_icicle_marker_colorbar_tickformatstop()}}{\code{icicle.marker.colorbar.tickformatstop}}
\item{\code{go_icicle_marker_colorbar_title()}}{\code{icicle.marker.colorbar.title}}
\item{\code{go_icicle_marker_colorbar_title_font()}}{\code{icicle.marker.colorbar.title.font}:
Sets this color bar's title font.}
\item{\code{go_icicle_marker_line()}}{\code{icicle.marker.line}}
\item{\code{go_icicle_marker_pattern()}}{\code{icicle.marker.pattern}:
Sets the pattern within the marker.}
\item{\code{go_icicle_outsidetextfont()}}{\code{icicle.outsidetextfont}:
Sets the font used for `textinfo` lying outside the sector. This option
refers to the root of the hierarchy presented on top left corner of a
treemap graph. Please note that if a hierarchy has multiple root nodes,
this option won't have any effect and `insidetextfont` would be used.}
\item{\code{go_icicle_pathbar()}}{\code{icicle.pathbar}}
